From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bigjakk <6015188+bigjakk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: kcc: do not emit per-packet input events nobody listens to

Stock behaviour (shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.cc):

    bool WebContents::PreHandleMouseEvent(...) {
      // |true| means that the event should be prevented.
      return Emit("before-mouse-event", event);
    }
    void WebContents::OnInputEvent(...) {
      Emit("input-event", event);
    }

Both run in the browser process on the UI thread for every input event
the widget receives (RenderWidgetHostImpl::ForwardMouseEventWithLatencyInfo
-> delegate_->PreHandleMouseEvent(), and the InputEventObserver list),
with no check that JavaScript has a listener. Each Emit()
(shell/browser/event_emitter_mixin.h) allocates an Event object,
converts the WebMouseEvent/WebInputEvent to a V8 object, and calls
emitter.emit() through node::MakeCallback() inside a
node::CallbackScope and a v8::MicrotasksScope(kRunMicrotasks). While
playing that is two such round trips per mouse packet, i.e. 2000-16000
per second with a 1000-8000 Hz mouse, on the thread that also routes
input to the renderer.

What the patch changes. It reuses the pattern Electron 45 already has
for 'console-message' (console_message_observed_ /
_setConsoleMessageObserved, maintained from the 'newListener' and
'removeListener' hooks at the end of WebContents.prototype._init in
lib/browser/api/web-contents.ts):

- two new bool members, before_mouse_event_observed_ and
  input_event_observed_, with setters bound as
  _setBeforeMouseEventObserved / _setInputEventObserved;
- the existing 'newListener' hook sets the matching flag when a
  listener for 'before-mouse-event' or 'input-event' is about to be
  added, and the existing 'removeListener' hook clears it when
  listenerCount() for that name drops to 0;
- with the feature enabled, PreHandleMouseEvent() returns false and
  OnInputEvent() returns before Emit() while the matching flag is
  false. No V8 work and no call into JavaScript happens per event; the
  cost is one bool test.

Return value: Emit() returns event.defaultPrevented. Without a listener
nothing can call preventDefault(), so the skipped call would have
returned false ("not handled"), which is what is returned. Once a
listener exists the stock Emit() runs and its result is returned
unchanged.

THIS PATCH CHANGES lib/ TYPESCRIPT (lib/browser/api/web-contents.ts, 8
added lines in the two existing hooks) and typings/internal-electron.d.ts
(2 declarations, needed by the electron_lib_typecheck build step). It
still applies with "git apply" from src/electron, but the browser JS
bundle has to be rebuilt, which the normal GN build does; a build that
reuses a prebuilt/stale JS bundle would leave the flags false forever.
The TS hooks run whether or not the feature is enabled (they only set
the two bools); the C++ event path is the stock one when it is off.

Gating: base::Feature KccSkipUnobservedInputEmits, disabled by default,
defined in the anonymous namespace of electron_api_web_contents.cc and
read once through a function-local static (hot path). With the feature
off both functions fall through to the stock Emit().

Behaviour differences with the feature ON (none when a listener is
registered with on/once/addListener/prependListener, including
events.once(webContents, ...)):
- Code that observes events without registering a listener, e.g. a
  monkey-patched webContents.emit, no longer sees 'before-mouse-event'
  or 'input-event'.
- webContents.removeAllListeners() with no argument also removes the
  internal 'newListener'/'removeListener' hooks (as it already does for
  'console-message' and the other internal listeners set up in _init),
  so a listener added afterwards would not turn the events back on.
  removeAllListeners('input-event') is fine.
- The microtask checkpoint and process.nextTick drain that each Emit()
  performed as a side effect no longer happen on input events.

Other design considered: probing the wrapper's _events[name] from C++
on every event. It needs no lib/ change and has no hook-lifetime caveat,
but it costs two V8 property lookups per event, depends on a Node.js
internal property, and is a new pattern; the flag matches existing
Electron code and is free per event.

A/B: --enable-features=KccSkipUnobservedInputEmits (or
app.commandLine.appendSwitch('enable-features', ...) before app ready).
The client must not have 'input-event'/'before-mouse-event' listeners
for the game window, otherwise nothing changes. Measure browser-process
main-thread CPU while moving a high-polling-rate mouse in the locked
game (ETW/perf or chrome://tracing "input" + "v8"): node::MakeCallback
and the gin converters should disappear from the mouse path. Also
check input latency / 1% lows. Functional check: with the feature on,
add a 'before-mouse-event' listener that calls preventDefault() and
confirm the page stops getting mouse events, remove it and confirm they
resume; same for an 'input-event' listener receiving events.

Platforms: all (browser process, UI thread). Not compiled, TypeScript
not type-checked here.

diff --git a/lib/browser/api/web-contents.ts b/lib/browser/api/web-contents.ts
index 1f7f125..c322dd6 100644
--- a/lib/browser/api/web-contents.ts
+++ b/lib/browser/api/web-contents.ts
@@ -429,11 +429,19 @@ WebContents.prototype._init = function () {
       // TODO(samuelmaddock): remove deprecated 'console-message' arguments
       if (listener.length > 1) consoleMessageDeprecated();
       if (!this.isDestroyed()) this._setConsoleMessageObserved(true);
+    } else if (eventName === 'before-mouse-event') {
+      if (!this.isDestroyed()) this._setBeforeMouseEventObserved(true);
+    } else if (eventName === 'input-event') {
+      if (!this.isDestroyed()) this._setInputEventObserved(true);
     }
   });
   this.on('removeListener' as any, (eventName: string | symbol) => {
     if (eventName === 'console-message' && !this.isDestroyed() && this.listenerCount('console-message') === 0) {
       this._setConsoleMessageObserved(false);
+    } else if (eventName === 'before-mouse-event' && !this.isDestroyed() && this.listenerCount('before-mouse-event') === 0) {
+      this._setBeforeMouseEventObserved(false);
+    } else if (eventName === 'input-event' && !this.isDestroyed() && this.listenerCount('input-event') === 0) {
+      this._setInputEventObserved(false);
     }
   });
 };
diff --git a/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.cc b/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.cc
index 65b5e51..f4bb0b0 100644
--- a/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.cc
+++ b/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.cc
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "base/containers/id_map.h"
 #include "base/containers/map_util.h"
 #include "base/environment.h"
+#include "base/feature_list.h"
 #include "base/files/file_util.h"
 #include "base/functional/callback_helpers.h"
 #include "base/json/json_reader.h"
@@ -470,6 +471,19 @@ bool g_disable_draggable_regions = false;
 // Number of WebContents with caret browsing enabled.
 int g_caret_browsing_count = 0;
 
+// KCC: when enabled, 'before-mouse-event' and 'input-event' are only emitted
+// while JavaScript has a listener for them (see |input_event_observed_|).
+// Stock Electron converts every input event to a V8 object and calls into
+// JavaScript for both events whether or not anyone listens.
+BASE_FEATURE(kKccSkipUnobservedInputEmits, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+
+// Input events are a hot path, so the feature state is read once.
+bool SkipUnobservedInputEmits() {
+  static const bool enabled =
+      base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kKccSkipUnobservedInputEmits);
+  return enabled;
+}
+
 void AdjustCaretBrowsingCount(int delta) {
   // g_caret_browsing_count should never be negative. This shouldn't be
   // possible, but it's cheap to ensure and log in dev.
@@ -1886,6 +1900,10 @@ bool WebContents::PlatformHandleKeyboardEvent(
 
 bool WebContents::PreHandleMouseEvent(content::WebContents* source,
                                       const blink::WebMouseEvent& event) {
+  // KCC: without a listener nobody can call preventDefault(), so the result
+  // of the emit would be |false|.
+  if (!before_mouse_event_observed_ && SkipUnobservedInputEmits())
+    return false;
   // |true| means that the event should be prevented.
   return Emit("before-mouse-event", event);
 }
@@ -4984,6 +5002,8 @@ void WebContents::PDFReadyToPrint() {
 void WebContents::OnInputEvent(const content::RenderWidgetHost& rfh,
                                const blink::WebInputEvent& event,
                                input::InputEventSource source) {
+  if (!input_event_observed_ && SkipUnobservedInputEmits())
+    return;
   Emit("input-event", event);
 }
 
@@ -5793,6 +5813,9 @@ void WebContents::FillObjectTemplate(v8::Isolate* isolate,
       .SetMethod<&WebContents::Clone>("clone")
       .SetMethod<&WebContents::SetConsoleMessageObserved>(
           "_setConsoleMessageObserved")
+      .SetMethod<&WebContents::SetBeforeMouseEventObserved>(
+          "_setBeforeMouseEventObserved")
+      .SetMethod<&WebContents::SetInputEventObserved>("_setInputEventObserved")
       .SetMethod<&WebContents::LoadURL>("loadURL")
       .SetMethod<&WebContents::Reload>("reload")
       .SetMethod<&WebContents::ReloadIgnoringCache>("reloadIgnoringCache")
diff --git a/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.h b/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.h
index 37c5ec2..e953306 100644
--- a/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.h
+++ b/shell/browser/api/electron_api_web_contents.h
@@ -473,6 +473,12 @@ class WebContents final : public ExclusiveAccessContext,
   void SetConsoleMessageObserved(bool observed) {
     console_message_observed_ = observed;
   }
+  void SetBeforeMouseEventObserved(bool observed) {
+    before_mouse_event_observed_ = observed;
+  }
+  void SetInputEventObserved(bool observed) {
+    input_event_observed_ = observed;
+  }
   void SetOwnerWindow(content::WebContents* web_contents,
                       NativeWindow* owner_window);
   void SetOwnerBaseWindow(std::optional<BaseWindow*> owner_window);
@@ -923,6 +929,11 @@ class WebContents final : public ExclusiveAccessContext,
   // Kept by JS while 'console-message' has listeners.
   bool console_message_observed_ = false;
 
+  // Kept by JS while 'before-mouse-event' / 'input-event' have listeners.
+  // Only consulted when the KccSkipUnobservedInputEmits feature is enabled.
+  bool before_mouse_event_observed_ = false;
+  bool input_event_observed_ = false;
+
   // Whether this WebContents currently contributes to the process-wide caret
   // browsing refcount.
   bool caret_browsing_counted_ = false;
